Error case: no --exercise at all, so Kong reports the missing flag as a usage error (exit 2) before any request. The nil guard in Validate leaves that message alone.
-- args --
activity
exercise-sets
set
12345678
-- table stdout --
-- table stderr --
Usage: gccli activity exercise-sets set --exercise=EXERCISE,... <id>

Set exercise sets for a strength training activity.

Arguments:
  <id>    Activity ID.

Flags:
  -h, --help                     Show context-sensitive help.
  -j, --json                     Output as JSON ($GCCLI_JSON).
      --plain                    Output as plain text (TSV) ($GCCLI_PLAIN).
      --header                   Print the column names as the first line of
                                 --plain output ($GCCLI_HEADER).
      --color="auto"             Color mode: auto, always, never ($GCCLI_COLOR).
      --account=STRING           Garmin account email ($GCCLI_ACCOUNT).
      --units="auto"             Unit system for distances, speeds, paces,
                                 elevations and weights in table and plain
                                 output: auto (Garmin profile), metric,
                                 statute_us, statute_uk ($GCCLI_UNITS).
      --version                  Print version information.

  -e, --exercise=EXERCISE,...    Exercise set in format
                                 CATEGORY/NAME:reps@weightkg[:dSECS][:rSECS]
                                 (e.g.
                                 BENCH_PRESS/BARBELL_BENCH_PRESS:12@20:d30:r60).

